# Milestone: v0.11.4-cat-f (T39 residual)
# Covers: the chk host-driver can register a native C function as a script
#         global, have a fixture call it, and assert the observed call count
#         via the `## host: expect-host-call <n>` directive.
#
# matrix-row: gc-finalizer
#
# This is the generic host-callback-assertion path.  The driver pre-registers
# a counting native global `__hostprobe` (urbi_register) before reading the
# fixture; each script-side call bumps the driver's counter; `expect-host-call`
# emits the running count as "host-calls: <n>" for the runner to diff.
#
# The finalizer->host-fn variant (a GC destroy callback observable from a
# fixture) is NOT exercised here — see finalizer_native.chk for why that path
# stays blocked.  This fixture proves the host-callback observation mechanism
# itself works against a directly-callable native global.
#
## host: expect-host-call 0
## host: run __hostprobe()
## host: expect-host-call 1
## host: run __hostprobe(); __hostprobe()
## host: expect-host-call 3
[00000000] host-calls: 0
[00000000] nil
[00000000] host-calls: 1
[00000000] nil
[00000000] host-calls: 3
